# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "    The `LayerError.error` attribute of the noise learning result contains the generators and error rates of the fitted Pauli Lindblad model, which has the form\n"
msgstr "L'attributo `LayerError.error` del risultato dell'apprendimento del rumore contiene i generatori e i tassi di errore del modello di Pauli-Lindblad adattato, che ha la forma\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "    $$ \\Lambda(\\rho) = \\exp{\\sum_j r_j \\left(P_j \\rho P_j^\\dagger - \\rho\\right)}, $$\n"
msgstr "    $$ \\Lambda(\\rho) = \\exp{\\sum_j r_j \\left(P_j \\rho P_j^\\dagger - \\rho\\right)}, $$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "    where the $r_j$ are the `LayerError.rates` and $P_j$ are the Pauli operators specified in `LayerError.generators`.\n"
msgstr "dove gli $r_j$ sono i `LayerError.rates` e i $P_j$ sono gli operatori di Pauli specificati in `LayerError.generators`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "    ### Noise learning options\n"
msgstr "    ### Opzioni di apprendimento del rumore\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "    You can choose among several options to input when you instantiate a `NoiseLearner` object. These options are encapsulated by the `qiskit_ibm_runtime.options.NoiseLearnerOptions` class and include the ability to specify the maximum layers to learn, number of randomizations, and the twirling strategy, among others. Refer to the [`NoiseLearnerOptions`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-models-noise-learner-v3-options) API documentation for detailed information.\n"
msgstr "Puoi scegliere tra diverse opzioni da specificare quando istanzi un oggetto `NoiseLearner`. Queste opzioni sono racchiuse nella classe `qiskit_ibm_runtime.options.NoiseLearnerOptions` e includono la possibilità di specificare il numero massimo di layer da apprendere, il numero di randomizzazioni e la strategia di twirling, tra le altre. Per informazioni più dettagliate, consulta la documentazione API su [`NoiseLearnerOptions`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-models-noise-learner-v3-options).\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "    Following is a simple example that shows how to use the `NoiseLearnerOptions` in a `NoiseLearner` experiment:\n"
msgstr "Di seguito è riportato un semplice esempio che mostra come usare `NoiseLearnerOptions` in un esperimento con `NoiseLearner`:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```python noexec\n"
"    # Build a GHZ circuit\n"
"    circuit = QuantumCircuit(10)\n"
"    circuit.h(0)\n"
"    circuit.cx(range(0, 9), range(1, 10))\n"
"    # Choose a backend to run on\n"
"    service = QiskitRuntimeService()\n"
"    backend = service.least_busy()\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    # Transpile the circuit for execution\n"
"    pm = generate_preset_pass_manager(backend=backend, optimization_level=3)\n"
"    circuit_to_run = pm.run(circuit_to_learn)\n"
msgstr ""
"    # Transpile the circuit for execution\n"
"    pm = generate_preset_pass_manager(backend=backend, optimization_level=3)\n"
"    circuit_to_run = pm.run(circuit_to_learn)\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    # Instantiate a NoiseLearnerOptions object\n"
"    learner_options = NoiseLearnerOptions(\n"
"        max_layers_to_learn=3, num_randomizations=32, twirling_strategy=\"all\"\n"
"    )\n"
msgstr ""
"    # Instantiate a NoiseLearnerOptions object\n"
"    learner_options = NoiseLearnerOptions(\n"
"        max_layers_to_learn=3, num_randomizations=32, twirling_strategy=\"all\"\n"
"    )\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    # Instantiate a NoiseLearner object and execute the noise learning program\n"
"    learner = NoiseLearner(mode=backend, options=learner_options)\n"
"    job = learner.run([circuit_to_run])\n"
"    noise_model = job.result()\n"
"    ```\n"
msgstr ""
"    # Instantiate a NoiseLearner object and execute the noise learning program\n"
"    learner = NoiseLearner(mode=backend, options=learner_options)\n"
"    job = learner.run([circuit_to_run])\n"
"    noise_model = job.result()\n"
"    ```\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "    ### Input noise model to a primitive\n"
msgstr "    ### Fornire il modello di rumore a una primitiva\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "    The noise model learned on the circuit can also be used as an input to the IBM Quantum `EstimatorV2` primitive. This can be passed into the primitive a few different ways. The next three examples show how you can pass the noise model to the `estimator.options` attribute directly, by using a `ResilienceOptionsV2` object before instantiating an Estimator primitive, and by passing in an appropriately formatted dictionary.\n"
msgstr "Il modello di rumore appreso sul circuito può essere usato anche come input per la primitiva IBM Quantum `EstimatorV2`. Può essere passato alla primitiva in diversi modi. I tre esempi successivi mostrano come puoi passare il modello di rumore all'attributo `estimator.options` direttamente, tramite un oggetto `ResilienceOptionsV2` prima di istanziare una primitiva Estimator, oppure passando un dizionario nel formato corretto.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```python noexec\n"
"    # Option 1: Pass the noise model to the `estimator.options` attribute directly\n"
"    estimator = EstimatorV2(mode=backend)\n"
"    estimator.options.resilience.layer_noise_model = noise_model\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    # Option 2: Specify options through a ResilienceOptionsV2 object\n"
"    resilience_options = ResilienceOptionsV2(layer_noise_model=noise_model)\n"
"    estimator_options = EstimatorOptions(resilience=resilience_options)\n"
"    estimator = EstimatorV2(mode=backend, options=estimator_options)\n"
msgstr ""
"    # Option 2: Specify options through a ResilienceOptionsV2 object\n"
"    resilience_options = ResilienceOptionsV2(layer_noise_model=noise_model)\n"
"    estimator_options = EstimatorOptions(resilience=resilience_options)\n"
"    estimator = EstimatorV2(mode=backend, options=estimator_options)\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    # Option 3: Specify options by using a dictionary\n"
"    options_dict = {\n"
"        \"resilience_level\": 2,\n"
"        \"resilience\": {\"layer_noise_model\": noise_model},\n"
"    }\n"
msgstr ""
"    # Option 3: Specify options by using a dictionary\n"
"    options_dict = {\n"
"        \"resilience_level\": 2,\n"
"        \"resilience\": {\"layer_noise_model\": noise_model},\n"
"    }\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    estimator = EstimatorV2(mode=backend, options=options_dict)\n"
"    ```\n"
msgstr ""
"    estimator = EstimatorV2(mode=backend, options=options_dict)\n"
"    ```\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    After the noise model is passed into the `EstimatorV2` object, it can be used to run workloads and perform error mitigation as normal.\n"
"  </AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
msgstr ""
"    Una volta passato il modello di rumore all'oggetto `EstimatorV2`, questo può essere usato per eseguire workload ed effettuare la mitigazione degli errori normalmente.\n"
"  </AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"

